  "worked_solution": "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{xln\u2061a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}\u2061x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{5}\u2061x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln\u2061(5)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{xln\u2061(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
